{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.EndBaseChange","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.EndBaseChange","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.MatrixAlgebra","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.ToLin","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Polynomial","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.TensorProduct.Basis"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.nonempty_endBaseChangeEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.nonempty_endBaseChangeEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/EndBaseChange.lean#L84-L90","doc":"Basis-free form: for `M` finite and free over `R`, the endomorphism algebra\nbase-changes. Stated as `Nonempty` because the equivalence depends on a choice\nof basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.endBaseChangeEquiv_tmul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.endBaseChangeEquiv_tmul","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/EndBaseChange.lean#L74-L82","doc":"`endBaseChangeEquiv` is the canonical map: it sends `a ⊗ₜ f` to\n`a • f.baseChange A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.endBaseChangeEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.endBaseChangeEquiv","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/EndBaseChange.lean#L64-L72","doc":"Extension of scalars carries `End R M` to `End A (A ⊗[R] M)`, for `M` free\nwith a finite basis `b`. See `endBaseChangeEquiv_tmul` for the value on\ngenerators, which identifies this with the canonical map. ","signatureChunk":0}]}